From: Onur R. Bingol <obingol@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Find tl-expected for shared LIEF builds in LIEFConfig.cmake

When LIEF is built against an external tl-expected (LIEF_OPT_EXTERNAL_EXPECTED),
tl::expected is a PUBLIC link dependency of LIEF::LIEF. It therefore shows up in
INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES of both LIEFExport-static.cmake and
LIEFExport-shared.cmake.

LIEFConfig.cmake only called find_dependency(tl-expected) inside the static
branch of LIEF_load_targets(). For a shared build nothing loaded the
tl-expected package, so find_package(LIEF) failed at generate time with:

  The link interface of target "LIEF::LIEF" contains: tl::expected
  but the target was not found.

The find_path() fallback that followed only appended an include directory to
LIEF::LIEF and never created the tl::expected target, so it could not satisfy
the link interface. Replace it with find_dependency(tl-expected), which
provides both the target and its include directories. find_package() returns
early when the package was already found, so this is a no-op for static builds.

Vendored builds (LIEF_EXTERNAL_EXPECTED=0) are unaffected: the headers ship
with LIEF and the block is skipped.

diff --git a/cmake/LIEFConfig.cmake.in b/cmake/LIEFConfig.cmake.in
index a819c4f1..39346443 100644
--- a/cmake/LIEFConfig.cmake.in
+++ b/cmake/LIEFConfig.cmake.in
@@ -142,16 +142,14 @@ endif()
 # their own CMake config that would otherwise be found using `find_dependency`
 # Header-only library can be found relatively easily
 
+# tl::expected is a PUBLIC link dependency of LIEF::LIEF (see the top-level
+# CMakeLists.txt), so it also appears in the INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES of the
+# shared export. The static branch of LIEF_load_targets() already looks it up,
+# but the shared branch does not, hence the lookup here. find_package() returns
+# early if the package was already found, so this is a no-op for static builds.
 if(@LIEF_EXTERNAL_EXPECTED@)
-  find_path(TL_EXPECTED_INCLUDE_DIR tl/expected.hpp)
-  if(NOT TL_EXPECTED_INCLUDE_DIR)
-    set(LIEF_NOT_FOUND_MESSAGE "Could not find include directory with 'tl/expected.hpp'. Consider setting `TL_EXPECTED_INCLUDE_DIR` during CMake configuration")
-    set(LIEF_FOUND FALSE)
-    return()
-  endif()
-  set_property(TARGET LIEF::LIEF APPEND PROPERTY
-    INTERFACE_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${TL_EXPECTED_INCLUDE_DIR}"
-  )
+  include(CMakeFindDependencyMacro)
+  find_dependency(tl-expected)
 endif()
 
 if(@LIEF_EXTERNAL_SPAN@)
